Introduction
The wooden phone stand is a simple and useful product designed to hold a smartphone in a stable and convenient position. It is made using wooden pieces that are accurately measured, cut, joined, and finished. The project focuses on converting natural wood into a compact, functional, and attractive phone stand.
Objective
To design and fabricate a simple wooden phone stand.
To provide stable support for a smartphone.
To make use of natural and easily available materials.
To develop a low-cost and useful product.
To improve practical skills in measuring, cutting, drilling, and assembling wood.
Materials Used
Wooden pieces
Wooden board/block
Wood adhesive
Sandpaper
Measuring scale
Pencil/marker
Cutting tools
Drill and drill bits
Finishing material/paint (optional)
Working Principle
The phone stand works by supporting the smartphone at a suitable angle using the wooden base and supporting members. The front slot or support prevents the phone from sliding forward, while the inclined portion keeps the phone in a comfortable viewing position.
Wooden Base → Support Structure → Phone Slot → Stable Phone Position

Construction
Wooden pieces are selected according to the required dimensions.
The dimensions are marked using a measuring scale.
The wooden pieces are cut according to the design.
A slot/support is provided to hold the phone securely.
The required holes and joints are made carefully.
The surfaces are sanded to remove rough edges.
The wooden pieces are joined using suitable wood adhesive.
The stand is allowed to dry and become firmly fixed.
The completed stand is tested by placing a smartphone on it.
